.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt BOOT_BLOB 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm boot_blob
.Nd return a read-only boot-time blob
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Fn boot_blob root_dev kind
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm returns a read-only memory object with a copy of boot-time data.
.Fa root_dev
must be the
.Em RootDevice
capability with
.Dv ADMIN ,
exactly as for
.Xr mmio_create 2 .
.Fa kind
selects the payload:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Dv 1
The ACPI bundle.  Its first bytes are a header
.Sy { magic: u32, version: u16, header_size: u16, rsdp_phys: u64,
table_count: u32, directory_offset: u32 }
with magic
.Qq RAC1
(0x31434152), version 1, and a header size of 24.
At
.Em directory_offset
follow
.Em table_count
20-byte directory entries
.Sy { signature: [u8; 8], offset: u32, length: u32, reserved: u32 }
naming blob-relative payload offsets.
The payloads are verbatim copies of the RSDP (signature
.Qq RSD PTR ) ,
the XSDT/RSDT, and every top-level table the kernel can reach (FADT, MADT,
MCFG and friends); SSDT and DSDT are never copied.
.It Dv 2
The flattened device tree; absent on x86-64, so
.Er ENOENT .
.It Dv 3
The memory-map summary: the BootInfo regions as
.Sy raven_bootinfo::MemoryRegion
records, page padded; the first all-zero record ends the array.
.El
The returned handle carries
.Dv READ ,
.Dv MAP ,
.Dv DUP
and
.Dv TRANSFER .
It has no
.Dv WRITE
right and a mapping with
.Dv PROT_WRITE
is refused with
.Er EPERM .
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EPERM
No root capability with
.Dv ADMIN .
.It Er ENOENT
The requested blob does not exist on this platform.
.It Er EINVAL
Unknown kind.
.It Er EMFILE
The process handle table is full.
.El
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
